The Human-English sets \(x(y) = \bigsqcup_n i_{n\infty}(x_{n+1}(y_n))\) and defines \(\lambda\)-abstraction by applying \(j_\infty\) to a continuous functional, so that \(D_\infty\) models the \(\lambda\)-calculus. The \(\lambda\)-model is not formalized. The displayed application is the value of one summand of the isomorphism's embedding: `iInfTerm.apply`, on the tower note for [Theorem 4.4](../FunctionSpaceTower/1972_Theorem_4_4.md), evaluates the \(n\)-th summand of \(i_\infty\) at \(z\) as \(i_{n\infty}(x_{n+1}(j_{\infty n}(z)))\). **Theorem:** no — the \(\lambda\)-calculus model is not formalized. **Proof:** no — the application formula occurs as the action of `embInfInf`, not as a model.
